WHAT CHANGED FROM ebaca58e — ONE FILE, ONE FIELD, A CORRECTION OF THIS SEAT'S OWN ERROR
  engine/rl_after/one_source_selftest.py  `_contract_md5`
      5f5ffdfd93e8342fb5bceca34834212a  ->  5f5ffdfdf2ee67ac99f4076245c89558

  WHY. The two selftest pins have ASYMMETRIC LENGTHS:
      _contract_md5    (:490)  a FULL 32-char md5
      _per_entrant_md5 (:500)  an 8-char stamp
  install_pass1.py treated both as 8-char and replaced only the PREFIX inside the full pin, yielding
  new-prefix + OLD-tail — a hash that named the right file with the wrong bytes. HAZARD CLASS 1,
  right-name-wrong-file, produced by this seat.

  IT WAS CAUGHT BY THE GUARD ON ITS FIRST RUN: the selftest's FROZEN-RULER contract byte-untouched
  check failed and printed both values, selftest rc=1. Non-vacuity working exactly as intended — the
  defect was live for one run and never reached a filed figure.

  `l6/install_pass1.py` is CORRECTED so pass 2 cannot inherit it: the full pin is now read out of the
  source by regex and replaced whole, the asymmetry is documented in-file, and the verify assert now
  requires the literal `_contract_md5='<FULL>'` rather than a substring.

